Manual

     Welcome to FrontEnd v1.1, created on 28 December 1994, few Days and
     we'll get high <joke>.

     First of all: FrontEnd is NOT a Replacement for TrapDoor!

     FrontEnd welcomes the User to the System and shows them various Infor-
     mation. I recommend you take a Look at the included FrontEnd.pic.

     FrontEnd requires CNet 3.05c. It was written entirely in C and compiled
     to be 68000-compatible. If you wish to use a processor-specific version,
     don't hesitate to contact me. I didn't want to blow up the archive.

     To install copy FrontEnd into your PFiles: Directory and call it from
     anywhere within CNet. The terminal prompt must have been passed,
     otherwise MCI commands aren't interpreted, thus output will be single
     colour. Remember to use <CTRL-Q>#2, it's a CNet C PFile.

     There's nothing to configure. The complete output is currently fixed,
     this is subject to change in a later release.

     If any of your Users contacts you about "Carrier=0 in FrontEnd", please
     contact the author immediately.


History

     v1.0      04 November 1994    First public release.

     v1.2      28 December 1994    Recognizing of "No new Users" Flag does
                                   work now. Mind that the port-specific Flag
                                   is checked, not the ALL PORTS setting.
							Replaced MCI GetUsers through real
							variables.


